
ocaml-zstd

# generically:
# 1. compile type description, which defines Types functor
# 2. write typgen ml code using Cstubs_structs.write_c on the Types functor just compiled
##   - this generates an implementation of mtype Ctypes.TYPE, derived from the c lib we’re wrapping
##     i.e. it generates definitions for all the types declared in our typdesc.Types functor decl
##     generated defs depend on the c hdr of the lib we’re wrapping
# 3. compile and run that code to generate c_generated_types.c
# 4. compile and link c_generated_types.c
# 5. run c_generated_types.exe to generate c_generated_types.ml
## at this point we have ml type code derived from our typedesc by way of c code that makes sure it’s ok
## i.e. we went from ml typdesc, to C code, back to ml code

# * write fungen ml code - like the typgen code but emits both c and ml code, from the fndesc module
# to compile fndesc we need generated types from above, and applied Types functor
## i.e. the fndesc needs a concrete implementation of types, which we get by applying Types functor to the generated types
## NB the circularity - from the Types functor we derive a (default?) static implementation, to which we then apply the functor
## why does this work? because the OCaml values used to define the Types functor represent C types.

################
# https://github.com/mbacarella/mpg123/blob/077a72d922931eb46d4b4e5842b0426fa3c161b5/c/dune

# https://github.com/aantron/luv/blob/master/src/c/dune

# https://github.com/avsm/ocaml-yaml/tree/master/types/stubgen

## Steps:
# * Compile Types_description.cmx

# * libzstd__type_gen.ml - generates c from Type_description.Types
#   compile libzstd__type_gen.ml to libzstd__type_gen.exe
#   run libzstd__type_gen.exe to produce libzstd__c_cout_generated_types.c
#   compile libzstd__c_cout_generated_types.c to libzstd__c_cout_generated_types.exe
#   run libzstd__c_cout_generated_types.exe to gen libzstd__c_generated_types.ml
#   compile libzstd__c_generated_types.ml to zstd_stubs__Libzstd__c_generated_types.[cmo|cmx]

# zzz => libzstd__function_gen__Function_description__Functions.ml

#   link zstd_stubs.cmx
#        zstd_stubs__Libzstd__c_generated_types.[cmo|cmx]
#        zstd_stubs__Type_description.cmx
#        zstd_stubs__Types_generated.cmx
#        zstd_stubs__Function_description.cmx
#        zstd_stubs__Libzstd__function_gen__Function_description__Functions.cmx
#        to libzstd__function_gen__Function_description__Functions.exe

# libzstd__function_gen__Function_description__Functions.exe generates both:
#     libzstd__c_cout_generated_functions__Function_description__Functions.c
#     libzstd__c_generated_functions__Function_description__Functions.ml
# $ (cd _build/default/stubs && ./libzstd__function_gen__Function_description__Functions.exe c libzstd_stubs) > _build/default/stubs/libzstd__c_cout_generated_functions__Function_description__Functions.c
# $ (cd _build/default/stubs && ./libzstd__function_gen__Function_description__Functions.exe ml libzstd_stubs) > _build/default/stubs/libzstd__c_generated_functions__Function_description__Functions.ml

# * construct zstd_stubs.ml-gen (ns resolver)
#   - contains Zstd_stubs__Libzstd__c_generated_functions__Function_description__Functions, etc.
# * -o zstd_stubs.cmo -c -impl stubs/zstd_stubs.ml-gen
# * -o zstd_stubs.cmx -c -impl stubs/zstd_stubs.ml-gen
# 2. compile stubs/libzstd__type_gen.exe
#    deps: zstd_stubs.cmx, zstd_stubs__Libzstd__type_gen.cmx

